    "_doc": "How townsfolk spend their day on the town map (world/innerMap/townLife.js). Folk spawn and go about only within the town (its streets, edgeMargin tiles clear of the map's edge). watch: the fewest guards a place keeps (townsfolk guards count toward it; the rest are the lord's watchmen); nightWatchShare of them keep the night (and sleep the morning). periods: the hour each part of the day begins. schedule[role][period]: weights of what they do — home, work, errand, market, tavern, church, plaza, well, stroll, chat, play ('default' for roles not listed; guards keep posts and patrols instead). stay: seconds spent at each ([min, max]; a real minute is an hour). tendOutside: the chance a role works out front of its door instead of indoors. chat.lines: said by two neighbours stopping to talk, by part of the day, by role, or 'any' ({name} = the other).",
